Since $\lim_{r \to 0} \frac{(x+1)^{r+1} - x^{r+1}}{r} = \frac{x+1-x}{1} = 1$, we have
$$g(x) = \lim_{r \to 0} \exp \left( \frac{1}{r} \ln \left( \frac{(x+1)^{r+1} - x^{r+1}}{r} \right) \right) = \exp \left( \lim_{r \to 0} \frac{\ln \left( \frac{(x+1)^{r+1} - x^{r+1}}{r} \right)}{r} \right)$$
