$$ = \frac{(x+1) \ln(x+1) - x \ln(x)}{x+1 - x} = (x+1) \ln(x+1) - x \ln(x)$$
Thus, $g(x) = \exp((x+1) \ln(x+1) - x \ln(x)) = \exp(\ln(x+1)^{x+1} - \ln(x^x)) = \frac{(x+1)^{x+1}}{x^x}$.

